<p class="event-desc">
  The Utah State University Department of Plants, Soils and Climate is pleased to announce the return of the annual PSC Showcase on Monday, April 14.
  The event featured a keynote address, a student poster session, and a departmental awards presentation.
  The student poster session took place from 1:30 to 3:30 p.m. in the Eccles Conference Center, rooms 307-313, highlighting research across the PSC department.
  Graduate students, undergraduate researchers, and interns presented on topics including soil health, plant biology, and climate modeling and prediction.
  The event also featured a keynote address by Dr. Mark Slavens, a USU alumnus and industry executive.
  A short awards presentation recognizing recent departmental and college-level award recipients immediately followed the keynote.
  The event was open to all students, faculty, and members of the PSC community.
  The keynote address took place at 10:30 a.m. in the Eccles Business Building, room 215.
  For more information, contact the PSC Department office at (435) 797-2233.
</p>
